- doctrine/DoctrineMongoDBBundle#994: registers the same service as `doctrine_mongodb.odm.collection_denormalizer`.

All three guard on `class_exists(CollectionDenormalizer::class)`, so they stay inert until 8.2 is released.

One point about the shape of the result. The retained implementation injects a whole collection object: the elements are denormalized, the collection is built from them, and the property is written with that collection. With adders and removers, the elements are added one by one instead, which is how collections are handled today. The core keeps that element by element path as long as the write target accepts an array, and only builds the collection class when the target rejects one. On the API Platform side the collection class is requested whenever the property declares one and the class is available, so that distinction is not applied yet.

